Package: sni-collector
Version: VERSION_PLACEHOLDER
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: ARCH_PLACEHOLDER
Depends: libpcap0.8t64 | libpcap0.8, adduser, systemd
Maintainer: Andrey (amix) <amix@amix.kiev.ua>
Homepage: https://github.com/amix/sni-collector
Description: Passive TLS SNI collector for proxy-bound traffic
 sni-collector is a lightweight, purely passive packet-capture tool for a
 Linux host that sits in front of a known HTTP/HTTPS proxy. It watches the
 TCP traffic containers or other applications send to that proxy,
 reassembles TLS ClientHello messages via TCP stream reassembly, and logs
 the SNI (server_name) each connection requested.
 .
 It never modifies, delays, drops, or originates any network traffic: it
 only reads from a passive libpcap capture, filtered at the kernel (BPF)
 level to the configured proxy IP:port. No TLS decryption, no MITM, no
 HTTP inspection, and no full-traffic DPI are performed.
